    ctos.ctos_end_date AS order_end_date COMMENT = 'Recorded end of the CTO period. A temporary hospital recall is separate and does not automatically end the order. Null does not prove the order is currently in force.',
    ctos.ctos_end_reason AS order_end_reason_description COMMENT = 'Recorded reason the CTO ended, where labelled. Missing or unmatched reasons remain unknown.',
    recalls.recalls_provider_code AS provider_organisation_code COMMENT = 'Code of the provider reporting these CTO recalls. Use for provider comparisons; codes are more stable grouping keys than names.',
    recalls.recalls_provider_name AS provider_organisation_name COMMENT = 'Name of the provider reporting these CTO recalls. Use for provider comparisons; a missing name does not mean the provider code is absent.',
    recalls.recalls_period_end AS reporting_period_end_date COMMENT = 'Reporting-period end attached to these CTO recalls. Use for submission evidence and freshness; use the recorded event date for when care or a change occurred.',
    recalls.recalls_start_date AS recall_start_date COMMENT = 'Recorded start of a hospital recall under a CTO. One order can have several separate recalls.',
    recalls.recalls_end_date AS recall_end_date COMMENT = 'Recorded end of the CTO recall. This is not necessarily the end of the underlying order; missing values remain unknown.',
    restrictive_incidents.restrictive_incidents_provider_code AS provider_organisation_code COMMENT = 'Code of the provider reporting these restrictive incidents. Use for provider comparisons; codes are more stable grouping keys than names.',
    restrictive_incidents.restrictive_incidents_provider_name AS provider_organisation_name COMMENT = 'Name of the provider reporting these restrictive incidents. Use for provider comparisons; a missing name does not mean the provider code is absent.',
    restrictive_incidents.restrictive_incidents_period_end AS reporting_period_end_date COMMENT = 'Reporting-period end attached to these restrictive incidents. Use for submission evidence and freshness; use the recorded event date for when care or a change occurred.',
    restrictive_incidents.restrictive_incidents_reason AS incident_reason_description COMMENT = 'Provider-recorded reason for a restrictive-intervention incident. It describes the submitted category, not a judgement that the intervention was justified.',
    restrictive_incidents.restrictive_incidents_start_date AS incident_start_date COMMENT = 'Recorded start date of the restrictive incident. Use for incident trends; reporting periods describe when evidence was submitted.',
    restrictive_types.restrictive_types_provider_code AS provider_organisation_code COMMENT = 'Code of the provider reporting these restrictive interventions. Use for provider comparisons; codes are more stable grouping keys than names.',
    restrictive_types.restrictive_types_provider_name AS provider_organisation_name COMMENT = 'Name of the provider reporting these restrictive interventions. Use for provider comparisons; a missing name does not mean the provider code is absent.',
    restrictive_types.restrictive_types_period_end AS reporting_period_end_date COMMENT = 'Reporting-period end attached to these restrictive interventions. Use for submission evidence and freshness; use the recorded event date for when care or a change occurred.',
    restrictive_types.restrictive_types_type AS intervention_type_description COMMENT = 'Type of restrictive intervention recorded within an incident. Several type occurrences can belong to one incident, so intervention counts and incident counts differ.',
    restrictive_types.restrictive_types_patient_injury AS patient_injury_description COMMENT = 'Reported patient-injury category associated with the intervention. Null must not be interpreted as no injury.',
    restrictive_types.restrictive_types_start_date AS intervention_start_date COMMENT = 'Recorded start date of the intervention occurrence. Use for intervention trends rather than incident counts.',
    home_leave.home_leave_provider_code AS provider_organisation_code COMMENT = 'Code of the provider reporting these home leave. Use for provider comparisons; codes are more stable grouping keys than names.',
    home_leave.home_leave_provider_name AS provider_organisation_name COMMENT = 'Name of the provider reporting these home leave. Use for provider comparisons; a missing name does not mean the provider code is absent.',
    home_leave.home_leave_period_end AS reporting_period_end_date COMMENT = 'Reporting-period end attached to these home leave. Use for submission evidence and freshness; use the recorded event date for when care or a change occurred.',
    home_leave.home_leave_start_date AS leave_start_date COMMENT = 'Recorded start of this leave or absence period. Leave remains separate from the inferred inpatient occupancy calculation.',
    home_leave.home_leave_end_date AS leave_end_date COMMENT = 'Recorded end of the home-leave period. Missing end dates do not alone establish the patient''s current whereabouts.',
    leave.leave_provider_code AS provider_organisation_code COMMENT = 'Code of the provider reporting these leave of absence. Use for provider comparisons; codes are more stable grouping keys than names.',
    leave.leave_provider_name AS provider_organisation_name COMMENT = 'Name of the provider reporting these leave of absence. Use for provider comparisons; a missing name does not mean the provider code is absent.',
    leave.leave_period_end AS reporting_period_end_date COMMENT = 'Reporting-period end attached to these leave of absence. Use for submission evidence and freshness; use the recorded event date for when care or a change occurred.',
    leave.leave_start_date AS leave_start_date COMMENT = 'Recorded start of this leave or absence period. Leave remains separate from the inferred inpatient occupancy calculation.',
    leave.leave_end_reason AS leave_end_reason_description COMMENT = 'Recorded reason the leave or absence ended, where labelled. It does not automatically identify a hospital discharge.',
    awol.awol_provider_code AS provider_organisation_code COMMENT = 'Code of the provider reporting these absence without leave. Use for provider comparisons; codes are more stable grouping keys than names.',
    awol.awol_provider_name AS provider_organisation_name COMMENT = 'Name of the provider reporting these absence without leave. Use for provider comparisons; a missing name does not mean the provider code is absent.',
    awol.awol_period_end AS reporting_period_end_date COMMENT = 'Reporting-period end attached to these absence without leave. Use for submission evidence and freshness; use the recorded event date for when care or a change occurred.',
    awol.awol_start_date AS leave_start_date COMMENT = 'Recorded start of this leave or absence period. Leave remains separate from the inferred inpatient occupancy calculation.',
    awol.awol_end_reason AS leave_end_reason_description COMMENT = 'Recorded reason the leave or absence ended, where labelled. It does not automatically identify a hospital discharge.',
    spell_commissioners.spell_commissioners_provider_code AS provider_organisation_code COMMENT = 'Code of the provider reporting these commissioner assignments. Use for provider comparisons; codes are more stable grouping keys than names.',
    spell_commissioners.spell_commissioners_provider_name AS provider_organisation_name COMMENT = 'Name of the provider reporting these commissioner assignments. Use for provider comparisons; a missing name does not mean the provider code is absent.',
    spell_commissioners.spell_commissioners_period_end AS reporting_period_end_date COMMENT = 'Reporting-period end attached to these commissioner assignments. Use for submission evidence and freshness; use the recorded event date for when care or a change occurred.',
    spell_commissioners.spell_commissioners_commissioner AS commissioner_organisation_name COMMENT = 'Organisation recorded as responsible for commissioning during this assignment period. Several commissioners or overlapping assignments can occur within one spell.',
    spell_commissioners.spell_commissioners_start_date AS commissioner_start_date COMMENT = 'Recorded start of the commissioner assignment. Use with the assignment period rather than applying one commissioner to the whole admission.',
    readiness.readiness_provider_code AS provider_organisation_code COMMENT = 'Code of the provider reporting these discharge readiness. Use for provider comparisons; codes are more stable grouping keys than names.',
    readiness.readiness_provider_name AS provider_organisation_name COMMENT = 'Name of the provider reporting these discharge readiness. Use for provider comparisons; a missing name does not mean the provider code is absent.',
    readiness.readiness_period_end AS reporting_period_end_date COMMENT = 'Reporting-period end attached to these discharge readiness. Use for submission evidence and freshness; use the recorded event date for when care or a change occurred.',
    readiness.readiness_delay_reason AS delay_reason_description COMMENT = 'Reported reason for delay while the patient was clinically ready for discharge. A changed reason can create another readiness period within the same admission.',
    readiness.readiness_attribution AS delay_attribution_description COMMENT = 'Reported attribution of the discharge delay. Describes the submitted category, not an independent judgement of responsibility.',
    readiness.readiness_start_date AS readiness_start_date COMMENT = 'Date the patient was recorded as clinically ready for discharge for this reason period. It is not the admission date.',
    readiness.readiness_end_date AS readiness_end_date COMMENT = 'Recorded end of this readiness period. The patient may have ceased to be ready without discharge; do not use this as a discharge date.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_provider_code AS provider_organisation_code COMMENT = 'Code of the provider reporting ward capacity. Use with local ward code and site to compare ward history; codes can change or be reused.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_provider_name AS provider_organisation_name COMMENT = 'Name of the provider reporting ward capacity. A missing name does not mean the provider code is absent.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_period_end AS reporting_period_end_date COMMENT = 'End of the accepted reporting period described by this snapshot. Select one period for a point-in-time comparison; summing periods repeats the underlying people, referrals or wards.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_site AS ward_site_name COMMENT = 'Recorded site containing the ward. Group by this to describe reported capacity at a site; missing site labels remain unknown.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_site_code AS ward_site_code COMMENT = 'Recorded organisation site code. Use with provider and local ward code to distinguish wards.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_local_ward_code AS ward_local_id COMMENT = 'Provider-local ward code. Group by provider and site as well; this code alone does not identify a ward across providers.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_setting AS ward_setting_description COMMENT = 'Recorded ward setting category. Describes the ward, not a currency-selected care setting.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_age_group AS ward_intended_age_group_description COMMENT = 'Age group the ward is intended to serve. It is not the actual age distribution of patients occupying beds.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_intended_sex AS ward_intended_sex_description COMMENT = 'Sex of patients the ward is intended to serve, not the actual mix of patients in the reporting period.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_care_intensity AS ward_clinical_care_intensity_description COMMENT = 'Recorded intended clinical care intensity of the ward. This describes its purpose, not individual patient acuity.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_security_level AS ward_security_level_description COMMENT = 'Recorded ward security level. Describes the ward category, not an individual patient risk assessment.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_locked_indicator AS locked_ward_indicator_description COMMENT = 'Recorded locked status for a general, non-secure ward, concerning unauthorised entry or exit. Separate from security level. Missing means unknown.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_has_capacity AS has_reported_available_capacity COMMENT = 'True when available bed days were supplied, including an explicit zero. False means capacity is missing, not zero beds.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_has_stay_evidence AS has_matching_ward_stay_evidence COMMENT = 'True when ward stays match the ward and submission. False means no matching stay evidence in this extract, not proof that beds were empty.',
    people.has_current_recorded_caseload AS has_current_recorded_caseload COMMENT = 'True when the person has an open referral in the dataset latest month. Includes community care and waiting for first attendance; it does not establish clinically active treatment.',
    latest_provider_caseload.latest_provider_caseload_provider AS provider_organisation_name COMMENT = 'Name of the provider reporting these open referrals from the latest provider submission. Use for provider comparisons; a missing name does not mean the provider code is absent.',
    latest_provider_caseload.latest_provider_caseload_evidence_date AS reporting_period_end_date COMMENT = 'Latest accepted reporting-period end for this provider, which can be older than the dataset latest month. Present this date with the provider caseload count.',
    latest_provider_caseload.latest_provider_caseload_months_behind AS provider_months_behind_dataset COMMENT = 'Calendar months between the provider''s latest accepted period and the dataset latest period. Zero means aligned with this feed, not necessarily with today. A gap alone does not prove a failed submission.'
)

METRICS(
    people.person_count AS COUNT(people.person_id) COMMENT = 'Number of identifiable MHSDS person IDs in all modelled evidence, including people with clinical-only records. One individual can have several national IDs over time.',
    people.current_inpatient_person_count AS COUNT_IF(people.is_current_inpatient) COMMENT = 'People with a retained open inpatient interval under the shared recency and overlap rules. Describes feed-based evidence, not live ward occupancy.',
    people.currently_detained_person_count AS COUNT_IF(people.is_currently_detained) COMMENT = 'People with at least one qualifying detention period: no end date, unexpired at as_of_date and reported within two calendar months of that date. Counts people once, not periods.',
    referrals.referral_count AS COUNT(referrals.source_record_id) COMMENT = 'Number of latest recorded service requests, including referrals without a person ID. Use referral_received_date for intake trends and referral_periods for historical state.',
    referrals.referral_person_count AS COUNT(DISTINCT referrals.person_id) COMMENT = 'Distinct non-null MHSDS person IDs across the selected referrals. National ID changes can split a person; do not add distinct counts across periods or providers.',
    referrals.mean_days_to_first_attended_contact AS AVG(referrals.days_to_first_attended_contact) COMMENT = 'Average calendar days from recorded referral receipt to first attended contact, among referrals with a valid observed interval. Referrals without an observed interval are excluded; this is not the average wait of everyone referred or a target-compliance measure.',
    referrals.referrals_with_observed_first_attendance AS COUNT(referrals.days_to_first_attended_contact) COMMENT = 'Referrals with a valid non-null receipt-to-first-attendance interval. This is the denominator of mean_days_to_first_attended_contact, not all referrals.',
    contacts.contact_count AS COUNT(contacts.source_record_id) COMMENT = 'Number of latest referral/contact pairs in all attendance states, including cancellations and non-attendance. Use contact_date for activity trends; use attended_contact_count for attended contacts.',
    contacts.attended_contact_count AS COUNT_IF(contacts.is_attended) COMMENT = 'Number of contacts with attendance code 05 or 06. Missing and other attendance codes do not contribute.',
    contacts.dna_contact_count AS COUNT_IF(contacts.is_dna) COMMENT = 'Number of contacts classified as non-attendance under codes 03 or 07. These are appointments, not delivered contacts.',
    contacts.cancelled_contact_count AS COUNT_IF(contacts.is_cancelled) COMMENT = 'Number of contacts with cancellation code 02 or 04. Their contact date is the recorded scheduled date, not a delivery date.',
    contacts.contact_person_count AS COUNT(DISTINCT contacts.person_id) COMMENT = 'Distinct non-null MHSDS person IDs in the selected contacts. Do not add monthly or team-level distinct counts; the same person can appear in several groups.',
    spells.recorded_spell_count AS COUNT(spells.source_record_id) COMMENT = 'Number of latest provider-recorded hospital spells before inferred occupancy rules. Use admission date for recorded admissions; overlapping or duplicated admissions can remain.',
    occupancy.occupancy_interval_count AS COUNT(occupancy.occupancy_interval_id) COMMENT = 'Number of inpatient intervals retained after shared duplicate, overlap and stale-submission rules. This is not a count of raw provider spells or occupied bed days.',
    occupancy.current_occupancy_count AS COUNT_IF(occupancy.is_current_inpatient) COMMENT = 'Retained inpatient intervals classified as open by the shared rules. Use the evidence date when presenting the count; this is not live occupancy.',
    diagnoses.diagnosis_record_count AS COUNT(diagnoses.diagnosis_record_id) COMMENT = 'Number of retained diagnosis evidence items, including undated or unlabelled records. Repeated or different diagnoses for a person can contribute several rows; this is not condition prevalence.',
    diagnoses.diagnosis_person_count AS COUNT(DISTINCT diagnoses.person_id) COMMENT = 'Distinct non-null MHSDS person IDs with the selected recorded diagnosis evidence. It does not establish clinically current disease prevalence.',
    assessments.assessment_observation_count AS COUNT(assessments.assessment_observation_id) COMMENT = 'Number of assessment response observations. A row can be a question, dimension or score; repeated accepted referral/activity occurrences remain. Do not call this completed questionnaires.',
    assessments.scored_observation_count AS COUNT(assessments.assessment_score_numeric) COMMENT = 'Assessment observations with a valid interpreted numeric score. Recognised non-score values and unmatched responses are excluded. It does not measure improvement.',
    legal_status.legal_status_period_count AS COUNT(legal_status.mental_health_act_period_id) COMMENT = 'Number of retained legal-status periods across all statuses, including informal, unknown and non-detention statuses. Filter is_detention_period for recorded detention periods.',
    submissions.accepted_submission_count AS SUM(submissions.n_accepted_submissions) COMMENT = 'Number of accepted files across selected provider periods. Use submissions.is_latest_provider_period for the latest file evidence per provider.',
    submissions.submitted_referral_row_count AS SUM(submissions.n_referral_source_records) COMMENT = 'Referral source rows across selected accepted submissions, before latest-version selection. Monthly repetition is included; this is not new referral intake.',
    submissions.submitted_contact_row_count AS SUM(submissions.n_contact_source_records) COMMENT = 'Contact source rows across selected accepted submissions, before latest-version selection. Reporting month is not contact activity month.',
    demographics.person_provider_period_count AS COUNT(demographics.person_provider_period_id) COMMENT = 'Number of person/provider/reporting-period snapshots. One person can contribute several providers and periods; this is not a distinct-person headcount.',
    referral_periods.referral_period_count AS COUNT(referral_periods.referral_period_id) COMMENT = 'Number of referral/submission snapshots. The same referral can appear each month. Select one reporting period for a snapshot count.',
    caseload_referrals.current_caseload_referral_count AS COUNT(caseload_referrals.referral_period_id) COMMENT = 'Recorded open referrals in the dataset latest accepted month, including those without attendance or person identity. Older provider submissions do not contribute.',
    caseload_people.current_caseload_person_provider_count AS COUNT(caseload_people.caseload_person_provider_id) COMMENT = 'Person/provider combinations with an open referral in the dataset latest month. A person at two providers counts twice; use current_caseload_person_count for a cross-provider headcount.',
    rtt.rtt_evidence_count AS COUNT(rtt.referral_to_treatment_period_id) COMMENT = 'Accepted RTT source records, including repeated period evidence of a clock. It does not count distinct waiting pathways or patients meeting a national waiting standard.',
    indirect_activity.indirect_activity_count AS COUNT(indirect_activity.indirect_activity_id) COMMENT = 'Accepted records of care without the patient present. Repeated reporting-period occurrences remain; this is not a deduplicated lifetime event count.',
    group_sessions.group_session_count AS COUNT(group_sessions.group_session_id) COMMENT = 'Accepted anonymous group-session records. Count sessions, not participants; repeated reporting-period records remain separate.',
    group_therapy.group_therapy_contact_count AS COUNT(group_therapy.group_therapy_contact_id) COMMENT = 'Patient contacts marked as group therapy, in all attendance states. Already included in contact_count; do not add them again or treat the count as sessions.',
    drop_ins.drop_in_contact_count AS COUNT(drop_ins.drop_in_contact_id) COMMENT = 'Accepted anonymous drop-in contact records. There is no patient ID, so this is a contact count rather than distinct people.',
    accommodation.accommodation_evidence_count AS COUNT(accommodation.accommodation_observation_id) COMMENT = 'Accepted accommodation observations, including repeated monthly reports. This does not count distinct people, moves or new housing episodes.',
    employment.employment_evidence_count AS COUNT(employment.employment_observation_id) COMMENT = 'Accepted employment observations, including repeated monthly reports. This does not count jobs, distinct people or changes in employment.',
    disability.disability_evidence_count AS COUNT(disability.disability_observation_id) COMMENT = 'Accepted disability observations, including multiple disabilities and repeated period reports per person. This is not disability prevalence.',
    social_circumstances.social_circumstance_evidence_count AS COUNT(social_circumstances.social_circumstance_observation_id) COMMENT = 'Accepted social/personal circumstance observations, including repeated reports. This does not count distinct people or newly occurring circumstances.',
    care_plans.care_plan_snapshot_count AS COUNT(care_plans.care_plan_period_id) COMMENT = 'Accepted care-plan records in reporting periods. The same plan can be submitted repeatedly; this does not count distinct implemented or agreed plans.',
    care_plan_agreements.care_plan_agreement_count AS COUNT(care_plan_agreements.care_plan_agreement_id) COMMENT = 'Accepted care-plan agreement records. Multiple signatories and repeated reporting periods can contribute several rows for a plan.',
    complaints.presenting_complaint_count AS COUNT(complaints.presenting_complaint_id) COMMENT = 'Retained presenting-complaint items after version selection. Complaints can be symptoms and do not count formal diagnoses or distinct people.',
    assessment_instances.assessment_instance_count AS COUNT(assessment_instances.assessment_instance_id) COMMENT = 'Groups of responses sharing assessment identity or tool/context/time/assessor details. This grouping is not a count of confirmed completed questionnaires; inspect ambiguity flags.',
    score_changes.score_change_pair_count AS COUNT(score_changes.assessment_score_change_id) COMMENT = 'Eligible successive score pairs within the same person, provider, referral, context, concept and assessor. A person can contribute several pairs; missing or ambiguous observations are excluded before pairing.',
    ctos.community_treatment_order_count AS COUNT(ctos.community_treatment_order_id) COMMENT = 'Retained CTO order periods, not ordinary community referrals or current inpatient detentions. Renewal updates an order''s expiry; recalls are counted separately.',
    recalls.cto_recall_count AS COUNT(recalls.community_treatment_order_recall_id) COMMENT = 'Retained hospital recall periods under CTOs. One order can have several recalls; this is not a count of orders or distinct people.',
    restrictive_incidents.restrictive_incident_count AS COUNT(restrictive_incidents.restrictive_intervention_incident_id) COMMENT = 'Retained provider-qualified restrictive incidents. One incident can contain several intervention types; use this metric for incident totals.',
    restrictive_types.restrictive_type_count AS COUNT(restrictive_types.restrictive_intervention_type_id) COMMENT = 'Retained restrictive-intervention occurrences. Several can belong to one incident, so this is not an incident total.',
    home_leave.home_leave_period_count AS COUNT(home_leave.home_leave_id) COMMENT = 'Retained recorded home-leave periods. Does not deduct bed days or establish current whereabouts.',
    leave.leave_of_absence_period_count AS COUNT(leave.leave_of_absence_id) COMMENT = 'Retained recorded leave-of-absence periods. Does not deduct bed days or establish current whereabouts.',
    awol.absence_without_leave_count AS COUNT(awol.absence_without_leave_id) COMMENT = 'Retained recorded absence-without-leave periods. Does not establish distinct people, bed-day deductions or current whereabouts.',
    spell_commissioners.spell_commissioner_period_count AS COUNT(spell_commissioners.spell_commissioner_period_id) COMMENT = 'Recorded commissioner assignment periods during admissions. Multiple or overlapping assignments can contribute to one spell.',
    readiness.discharge_readiness_period_count AS COUNT(readiness.discharge_readiness_period_id) COMMENT = 'Recorded readiness-and-delay-reason periods. A changed reason can create another period; this is not a count of delayed discharges or delayed bed days.',
    ward_capacity.ward_capacity_period_count AS COUNT(ward_capacity.ward_capacity_period_id) COMMENT = 'Ward/submission capacity records. Select a single reporting period when comparing wards; rows can exist without reported available bed days.',
    caseload_people.current_caseload_person_count AS COUNT(DISTINCT caseload_people.person_id) COMMENT = 'Distinct non-null person IDs with an open referral in the dataset latest month across selected providers. Use this for headcount rather than summing provider headcounts.',
    caseload_referrals.caseload_referrals_without_attendance AS COUNT_IF(caseload_referrals.is_open_without_recorded_attendance) COMMENT = 'Current-month recorded open referrals with no attended contact evidenced by period end. Describes waiting for first recorded attendance, not national waiting-list eligibility.',
    referral_periods.open_referral_period_count AS COUNT_IF(referral_periods.is_recorded_open_at_period_end) COMMENT = 'Referral snapshots open at the selected period end. Select one reporting period for caseload; summing across periods counts the same referral repeatedly.',
    indirect_activity.recorded_indirect_activity_minutes AS SUM(indirect_activity.duration_minutes) COMMENT = 'Sum of submitted patient-perspective indirect-care duration in minutes. Repeated period records remain; missing duration is ignored, and totals are not staff workload hours.',
    group_sessions.recorded_anonymous_participations AS SUM(group_sessions.recorded_participant_count) COMMENT = 'Sum of recorded participants across anonymous group-session records. Counts participations, not distinct people. Do not add to identified contact counts.',
    group_therapy.attended_group_therapy_contact_count AS COUNT_IF(group_therapy.is_attended) COMMENT = 'Group-therapy patient contacts with attendance code 05 or 06. A subset of attended_contact_count, not additional activity or a count of sessions.',
    score_changes.mean_score_change AS AVG(score_changes.score_change) COMMENT = 'Mean of current minus previous score across eligible pairs. Filter to one assessment concept and instrument; do not average different scales or interpret the sign as universal improvement.',
    score_changes.mean_previous_score AS AVG(score_changes.previous_score) COMMENT = 'Mean previous score among eligible pairs for one selected concept and instrument. The previous score is not necessarily a baseline assessment.',
    score_changes.mean_current_score AS AVG(score_changes.current_score) COMMENT = 'Mean current score among eligible pairs for one selected concept and instrument. The current score is not necessarily a discharge or follow-up outcome.',
    ward_capacity.reported_available_bed_days AS SUM(ward_capacity.available_bed_days) COMMENT = 'Sum of monthly reported staffed bed days, whether occupied or unoccupied. Missing capacity is ignored rather than treated as zero. This is not spare beds or live availability.',
    ward_capacity.reported_closed_bed_days AS SUM(ward_capacity.temporarily_closed_bed_days) COMMENT = 'Sum of monthly reported temporarily closed staffed bed days. Missing values remain unknown; permanent closures are not this measure.',
    ward_capacity.total_reported_bed_base_days AS SUM(ward_capacity.reported_bed_base_days) COMMENT = 'Available plus temporarily closed bed days for wards reporting both components. Usually staffed capacity, or commissioned capacity for specialised beds. Excludes wards missing either value, permanent closures and unallocated independent-sector beds.',
    ward_capacity.ward_periods_with_available_capacity AS COUNT(ward_capacity.available_bed_days) COMMENT = 'Ward/submission records with reported available bed days, including explicit zero. Compare with ward_capacity_period_count to show coverage.',
    ward_capacity.ward_periods_with_complete_bed_base AS COUNT(ward_capacity.reported_bed_base_days) COMMENT = 'Ward/submission records reporting both available and temporarily closed bed days. Compare with ward_capacity_period_count to show coverage of reported bed base totals.',
    ward_capacity.reported_average_available_beds AS IFF(COUNT(DISTINCT ward_capacity.reporting_period_start_date) = 1 AND COUNT(DISTINCT ward_capacity.reporting_period_end_date) = 1, SUM(ward_capacity.average_available_beds), NULL) COMMENT = 'Average staffed beds available across reporting wards in one common period, including occupied beds. Null across multiple periods. Report coverage alongside this total; missing wards are excluded. Not live vacancies.',
    ward_capacity.reported_average_temporarily_closed_beds AS IFF(COUNT(DISTINCT ward_capacity.reporting_period_start_date) = 1 AND COUNT(DISTINCT ward_capacity.reporting_period_end_date) = 1, SUM(ward_capacity.average_temporarily_closed_beds), NULL) COMMENT = 'Average temporarily closed beds across reporting wards in one common period. Null across multiple periods. Missing closure counts are excluded, not treated as zero.',
    ward_capacity.reported_average_bed_base AS IFF(COUNT(DISTINCT ward_capacity.reporting_period_start_date) = 1 AND COUNT(DISTINCT ward_capacity.reporting_period_end_date) = 1, SUM(ward_capacity.average_reported_bed_base), NULL) COMMENT = 'Average reported bed base, including temporary closures, for wards reporting both components in one common period. Null across multiple periods. Show complete-bed-base coverage. Not a physical inventory or month-end count.',
    ward_capacity.recorded_ward_stay_midnight_count AS SUM(ward_capacity.recorded_ward_stay_midnights) COMMENT = 'Sum of recorded ward-stay midnights clipped to submission periods, including leave and possible overlaps. This extract may omit patients; zero can mean no matching stay evidence, not empty beds. Do not divide by reported capacity and call the result validated physical occupancy.',
    latest_provider_caseload.latest_provider_open_referral_count AS COUNT(latest_provider_caseload.referral_period_id) COMMENT = 'Open referrals from each provider''s latest accepted period, including stale periods. Provider dates can differ; use current_caseload_referral_count for a common dataset-latest month.'
)

COMMENT = 'MHSDS recorded care and monthly evidence. Choose the entity matching the question: referrals, contacts, diagnoses, assessments, current caseload, inferred occupancy or reported capacity. Each has its own row meaning and date basis. Measures describe this extract, not all lifetime care or live operational state.'
AI_SQL_GENERATION 'Return non-identifying aggregates only; never select person or patient identifiers in results. For current recorded caseload use caseload_referrals or caseload_people, which contain only the dataset latest accepted month. For each provider''s latest evidence including older months use latest_provider_caseload and report its evidence date and lag. For historical open referrals use referral_periods and select the reporting period. Use contact_date for contact activity and attendance filters for delivered care; group_therapy is already included in contacts. Anonymous group_sessions and drop_ins have no patient linkage or defensible join to identified sessions. For period demographics use only the declared relationships from referral_periods, caseload_referrals, caseload_people, indirect_activity or care_plans to demographics. People dimensions describe current evidence and must not be used as historical state. Filtering on people attributes restricts results to linked identifiable people. Cross-fact cohorts require separate aggregation to the intended person or referral grain before joining; joining several contacts to several diagnoses multiplies rows. National person IDs can change across submissions, so compare historical contact context before treating a later referral-ID disagreement as an error. For recorded admissions use spells; for inferred current inpatient evidence use occupancy or the people current-inpatient measure. Diagnoses count recorded evidence, assessments count responses, and assessment_instances are not confirmed completed questionnaires. Score-change means require one concept and instrument; neither sign nor magnitude establishes clinical improvement. Available bed days include occupied staffed beds and are not spare beds. For bed counts use the reported_average_available_beds, reported_average_temporarily_closed_beds or reported_average_bed_base metrics with one reporting period per result group. Report ward capacity coverage alongside totals; missing wards are excluded. The bed base includes temporary closures only where both components were reported. Missing capacity and unmatched ward stays must not become zero capacity or zero physical occupancy. Do not present recorded stay midnights divided by reported capacity as validated occupancy: the commissioning extract may omit patients and stays include leave or overlaps. Keep original complaint coding schemes; alternative labels are unconfirmed. Open referrals and RTT records do not by themselves establish national waiting-list eligibility or target compliance. Currency classification and costing are outside this view.'
AI_QUESTION_CATEGORIZATION 'Use this view for aggregate questions about MHSDS referrals and first recorded attendance, monthly recorded caseload, contacts and indirect care, anonymous or identified group activity, circumstances and care plans, recorded clinical and legal evidence, descriptive assessment scores, inpatient stays, discharge readiness, reported ward capacity and provider submission freshness. Cost questions need separate costing models; currency figures are estimates, not actual provider expenditure. The view cannot establish live bed availability, national waiting-time compliance, clinically current diagnoses or clinical improvement.'
